# Load a frozen single-class caster, give him one real level through the
# character sheet's free-advancement path (Player::AdvanceLevel, the same
# path a normal level-up takes), and photograph the sheet before and after.
# bd inc-ngku: a level-up with NO Intensive Study must still grant exactly
# the spellcasting chart's slots at the new raw class level.
#
# WHY THE WIZARD MENU. The fixture's XP is 0 and the settings fixture leaves
# Free Advancement off, so the sheet's G/A level command refuses. The wizard
# mode switch (Player::WizardOptions, src/Debug.cpp) turns Free Advancement on
# for this run, which is the only way a key script reaches AdvanceLevel without
# grinding XP. The load copies the save into the run sandbox, so the fixture
# itself is untouched.
#
# The character is the single-class Orc Mage 1 of
# tools/fixtures/chars/orc-mage-seed4-opt0822.sav: ClassID[1] is 0, so
# AdvanceLevel asks no class menu; its level-2 feat menu is answered with 'a'
# (the first entry), which the engine accepts as an ordinary choice.

@dump:arrival

s               # one real turn, so this counts as a session
@dump:played

w               # wizard mode
y               # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes
w               # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
DOWN DOWN
SPACE           # Free Advancement: NO -> YES
ESC

d               # character sheet
@expect "Class  Mage 1"
@dump:sheet-before

G               # [G]ain a level -- Player::AdvanceLevel
@until "Mage 2" a   # answer whatever level-up menu opens (feat pick) and
                    # let the sheet repaint to the new class line
@dump:sheet-after

ESC             # leave the sheet, back to play mode
@quit
